  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_water_activation",
  "label": "Children in water mapped to Sea-Monkeys 'coming to life' in water",
  "description": "A secondary analogical mapping that reinforces the primary racist comparison: the text 'sea monkeys' combined with the visual of children actively playing in shallow_coastal_water creates a parallel to the Sea-Monkeys toy product's marketing claim that the creatures 'come to life' when added to water. This mapping exploits the aquatic setting to strengthen the dehumanizing comparison, suggesting the children are like the toy organisms that activate in water. The water context is essential to making the Sea-Monkeys reference work as a racist 'joke'.",
